module

public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.Presheaf
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Coverage
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.BigSite.StructureSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SheafComparison
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.Functoriality

/-!
# The structure sheaf of the small crystalline site

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)`.  The structure presheaf `𝒪_{X/S}` of the
crystalline site sends a divided power thickening `(U, T, δ)` to the ring `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)` of global
sections of its ambient scheme.  A covering family of the small crystalline site `Cris(X/S)` is a
family of Cartesian morphisms `{(Uᵢ, Tᵢ, δᵢ) ⟶ (U, T, δ)}` whose ambient schemes form a Zariski
covering `{Tᵢ ⟶ T}`, so the descent condition for `𝒪_{X/S}` over such a family is the Zariski
sheaf condition for `𝒪_T` on `T`; the structure presheaf is therefore a sheaf.

The reduction proceeds in two steps.  Every covering family of `Cris(X/S)` is refined by the
family of restrictions of `(U, T, δ)` to the images of the `Tᵢ`, because a Cartesian morphism
which is an open immersion on ambient schemes is, over the image of that open immersion, an
isomorphism onto such a restriction; so the Zariski topology of the small crystalline site is the
topology generated by the coverage of families of restrictions to an open cover of the ambient
scheme.  For such a family the sections of the structure presheaf over the members are the
sections of `𝒪_T` over the members of the open cover, compatibly with restriction, and descent is
the sheaf condition for `𝒪_T`.

## Main definitions

Everything below lives in the namespace `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite`.

* `SmallSite.crisRing` — the structure presheaf of the small crystalline site, as a presheaf of
  rings, and `SmallSite.structurePresheaf` the same presheaf with values in commutative rings.
* `SmallSite.restrictCoverage` — the coverage of `Cris(X/S)` whose covering presieves are the
  families of restrictions of an object to an open cover of its ambient scheme.
* `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenLE` — the morphism between the restrictions of an
  object of `Cris(X/S)` to two nested opens of its ambient scheme, and
  `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenMap` the restriction of a morphism of `Cris(X/S)`
  over an open of the ambient scheme of its target.
* `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenFunctor` — the restrictions of an object of
  `Cris(X/S)` to the opens of its ambient scheme, as a functor from the Zariski site of that
  scheme to `Cris(X/S)`.
* `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.sectionsIso` — the sections of the structure presheaf over the
  restriction of an object to an open of its ambient scheme, identified with the sections of the
  structure sheaf of that scheme over that open.
* `SmallSite.structureSheaf` — the structure sheaf `𝒪_{X/S}` of the small crystalline site, and
  `SmallSite.commStructureSheaf` the same sheaf with values in commutative rings.

## Main results

* `SmallSite.restrictCoverage_toGrothendieck` — the Zariski topology of the small crystalline site
  is generated by the families of restrictions to an open cover of the ambient scheme.
* `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.isSheafFor_restrictOpenCover` — the structure presheaf satisfies
  descent for the family of restrictions of an object to an open cover of its ambient scheme.
* `SmallSite.isSheaf_crisRing` — the structure presheaf of the small crystalline site is a sheaf,
  and `SmallSite.isSheaf_structurePresheaf` the same with values in commutative rings.
* `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.exists_comp_restrictOpenHom_eq` — the universal property of the
  restriction of an object of `Cris(X/S)` to an open of its ambient scheme.
* `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenFunctor_isContinuous` and
  `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenFunctor_isCocontinuous` — the restrictions of an
  object of `Cris(X/S)` to the opens of its ambient scheme form a continuous and cocontinuous
  functor from the Zariski site of that scheme to the small crystalline site.
* `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.isSheaf_restriction` — the restriction of a sheaf on
  `Cris(X/S)` to the ambient scheme of an object is a Zariski sheaf on that scheme.

## Implementation notes

The sheaf condition is the one of `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.IsSheaf`, which for a presheaf of rings
is tested by composing with the functors corepresented by the rings; the Zariski sheaf condition
used on the ambient scheme is therefore `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ringCatSheaf`, the structure
sheaf of a scheme viewed as a sheaf of rings, in exactly the same form.  Replacing the generated
topology by a coverage is what makes the two conditions comparable: a coverage needs only that the
covering presieves be stable under pullback up to refinement, which for families of restrictions
is the restriction of a morphism over an open, and
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.isSheaf_coverage` then tests the sheaf condition on the covering presieves
of the coverage alone.

Everything this file constructs lives in `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite`,
including the additions to the `Thickening` and `CrystallineThickening` namespaces, which are
nested inside it.  The big and the small crystalline site share the namespace
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation`, and the two sites name the same constructions the same
way — a structure presheaf, its sheaf condition, the bundled sheaf — so a structure sheaf file for
the big site and one for the small site collide on every one of those names unless one of them is
namespaced away.  Do not flatten this namespace: the `SmallSite` prefix is what keeps these
declarations from clashing with the big site's.  Because that prefix already says `SmallSite`, the
names inside it drop the `small` that the small site's declarations in the shared namespace carry;
conversely the big site's `crisRing` and `structureSheaf` are written
`GlobalCrystallineSituation.crisRing` and `GlobalCrystallineSituation.structureSheaf` where this
file needs them, since unqualified those two now resolve to the small site's.

That the global sections of an open subscheme are the sections of the ambient scheme over that
open is `private` here.  It is a general fact about schemes with no crystalline content, and the
library states it twice already — `Stacks.LocalCohomology.ι_appTop_topIso_hom`, and a `private`
copy in `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Variety/Defs/Dimension/Formula.lean` — so a third public
copy would be a third name for one fact.  Keeping it private follows the precedent of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/ExplicitDividedPower/Formula.lean` and avoids
importing the local cohomology tree into the crystalline tree for a
single lemma.

That the restriction of a *sheaf* to the ambient scheme of an object is a Zariski sheaf is
continuity of `SmallSite.CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenFunctor`, not cocontinuity: restriction
along the opposite of a functor carries sheaves to sheaves exactly when the functor is continuous,
`CategoryTheory.Functor.op_comp_isSheaf_of_isSheaf`.  Continuity is obtained from
`CategoryTheory.Functor.isContinuous_of_coverPreserving`, whose compatible-preserving half rests on
the universal property of a restriction,
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.exists_comp_restrictOpenHom_eq`; that universal
property is why this file imports the big site's structure sheaf file, which is where the
identification of an object with its restriction to the whole ambient scheme lives.  Cocontinuity
is recorded alongside, so the pair exhibits the Zariski site of the ambient scheme as a site over
the small crystalline site in both directions.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IQ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

universe w v t u

noncomputable section

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **The sections of an open subscheme over its whole space are the sections of the ambient
scheme over that open**, compatibly with the map on sections of its open immersion. -/
private theorem Scheme.Opens.ι_appTop_topIso_hom {X : Scheme.{u}} (W : X.Opens) :
    W.ι.appTop ≫ (Scheme.Opens.topIso W).hom =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤)).op :=
  (X.presheaf.map_comp _ _).symm.trans (congrArg X.presheaf.map (Subsingleton.elim _ _))

end AlgebraicGeometry

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

variable {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}}

/-- The structure presheaf of the small crystalline site, as a presheaf of rings: it sends an
object `(U, T, δ)` of `Cris(X/S)` to the ring of global sections `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)`. -/
def crisRing (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u} :=
  (CrystallineThickening.ι S).op ⋙ GlobalCrystallineSituation.crisRing S

namespace Thickening

/-- **The map on sections of the structure morphism of a restriction is a restriction map of the
structure sheaf of the ambient scheme.** -/
theorem structureSheaf_map_restrictOpenHom (A : Thickening S)
    (W : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    (GlobalCrystallineSituation.structureSheaf S).map (A.restrictOpenHom W).op ≫
        (Thickening.restrictionStructureIso A).hom.app (op W) =
      A.thickening.target.scheme.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤)).op :=
  Scheme.Opens.ι_appTop_topIso_hom W

end Thickening

namespace CrystallineThickening

/-- **The morphism of `Cris(X/S)` between the restrictions of an object to two nested opens of its
ambient scheme**, the morphism of `CRIS(X/S)` between the restrictions of the underlying object. -/
def restrictOpenLE (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    {V V' : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens} (h : V ≤ V') :
    A.restrictOpen V ⟶ A.restrictOpen V' :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (A.obj.restrictOpenLE h)

/-- The underlying morphism of `CRIS(X/S)` of `restrictOpenLE A h` is `A.obj.restrictOpenLE h`. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrictOpenLE_hom (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    {V V' : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens} (h : V ≤ V') :
    (restrictOpenLE A h).hom = A.obj.restrictOpenLE h := rfl

/-- **Restricting an object of `Cris(X/S)` further is compatible with the structure morphisms of
the two restrictions.** -/
@[reassoc]
theorem restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    {V V' : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens} (h : V ≤ V') :
    restrictOpenLE A h ≫ A.restrictOpenHom V' = A.restrictOpenHom V :=
  ObjectProperty.hom_ext (Thickening.IsCrystalline (S := S))
    (A.obj.restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom h)

/-- The structure morphism of the restriction of an object of `Cris(X/S)` to an open of its
ambient scheme is a monomorphism, being one in `CRIS(X/S)`. -/
instance mono_restrictOpenHom (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    (V : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) : Mono (A.restrictOpenHom V) :=
  (CrystallineThickening.ι S).mono_of_mono_map
    (inferInstanceAs (Mono (A.obj.restrictOpenHom V)))

/-- **The restrictions of an object of `Cris(X/S)`, as a functor from the opens of its ambient
scheme to `Cris(X/S)`.** -/
def restrictOpenFunctor (A : CrystallineThickening S) :
    A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens ⥤ CrystallineThickening S where
  obj W := A.restrictOpen W
  map i := restrictOpenLE A i.le
  map_id _ := ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (by simp)
  map_comp _ _ := ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (by simp)

/-- The functor `restrictOpenFunctor A` sends an open `W` to the restriction `A.restrictOpen W`. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrictOpenFunctor_obj (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    (W : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    (restrictOpenFunctor A).obj W = A.restrictOpen W := rfl

/-- The functor `restrictOpenFunctor A` sends an inclusion of opens `W ≤ W'` to
`restrictOpenLE A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem restrictOpenFunctor_map (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    {W W' : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens} (i : W ⟶ W') :
    (restrictOpenFunctor A).map i = restrictOpenLE A i.le := rfl

/-- **The universal property of the restriction of an object of `Cris(X/S)` to an open `V` of its
ambient scheme:** a morphism into that object whose ambient scheme maps into `V` factors through
the restriction. -/
theorem exists_comp_restrictOpenHom_eq {A B : CrystallineThickening S}
    (V : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) (r : B ⟶ A)
    (hr : ∀ x : B.obj.thickening.target.scheme, r.hom.targetHom.hom.base x ∈ V) :
    ∃ p : B ⟶ A.restrictOpen V, p ≫ A.restrictOpenHom V = r :=
  let ⟨p, hp⟩ := Thickening.exists_comp_restrictOpenHom_eq V r.hom hr
  ⟨ObjectProperty.homMk p, ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ hp⟩

/-- **The restriction of a morphism of `Cris(X/S)` over an open of the ambient scheme of its
target**, the restriction of the morphism of `CRIS(X/S)` between the underlying objects. -/
def restrictOpenMap {A B : CrystallineThickening S} (g : A ⟶ B)
    (W : B.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    A.restrictOpen (g.hom.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ W) ⟶ B.restrictOpen W :=
  ObjectProperty.homMk (Thickening.restrictOpenMap g.hom W)

/-- **The restriction of a morphism of `Cris(X/S)` over an open of the ambient scheme of its
target is compatible with the structure morphisms of the two restrictions.** -/
@[reassoc]
theorem restrictOpenMap_restrictOpenHom {A B : CrystallineThickening S} (g : A ⟶ B)
    (W : B.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    restrictOpenMap g W ≫ B.restrictOpenHom W =
      A.restrictOpenHom (g.hom.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ W) ≫ g :=
  ObjectProperty.hom_ext (Thickening.IsCrystalline (S := S))
    (Thickening.restrictOpenMap_restrictOpenHom g.hom W)

/-- **The restriction of an object of `Cris(X/S)` to the image of a Cartesian open immersion into
it lies in every sieve containing that open immersion.**  Over that image the open immersion
restricts to an isomorphism onto the restriction. -/
theorem restrictOpenHom_opensRange_mem_generate {A B : CrystallineThickening S} (q : A ⟶ B)
    [IsOpenImmersion q.hom.targetHom.hom] (hq : Thickening.IsCartesian q.hom)
    {R : Presieve B} (hR : R q) :
    (Sieve.generate R).arrows (B.restrictOpenHom q.hom.targetHom.hom.opensRange) := by
  have : IsIso ((CrystallineThickening.ι S).map
      (restrictOpenMap q q.hom.targetHom.hom.opensRange)) :=
    Thickening.isIso_restrictOpenMap q.hom hq _ le_rfl
  have : IsIso (restrictOpenMap q q.hom.targetHom.hom.opensRange) :=
    isIso_of_fully_faithful (CrystallineThickening.ι S) _
  refine ⟨A, inv (restrictOpenMap q q.hom.targetHom.hom.opensRange) ≫
    A.restrictOpenHom (q.hom.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ q.hom.targetHom.hom.opensRange), q, hR, ?_⟩
  rw [Category.assoc, ← restrictOpenMap_restrictOpenHom q, IsIso.inv_hom_id_assoc]

/-- The structure sheaf of the ambient scheme of an object of `Cris(X/S)`, as a presheaf of
rings. -/
abbrev ambientRingPresheaf (A : CrystallineThickening S) :
    (A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)ᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u} :=
  A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.presheaf ⋙ forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}

/-- **The structure sheaf of rings of the ambient scheme of an object of `Cris(X/S)` is a sheaf
for the Zariski topology of that scheme.** -/
theorem isSheaf_ambientRingPresheaf (A : CrystallineThickening S) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology A.obj.thickening.target.scheme)
      (ambientRingPresheaf A) :=
  A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.ringCatSheaf.property

/-- **The sections of the structure presheaf of the small crystalline site over the restriction of
an object to an open of its ambient scheme are the sections of the structure sheaf of that scheme
over that open.** -/
def sectionsIso (A : CrystallineThickening S) (W : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    (crisRing S).obj (op (A.restrictOpen W)) ≅ (ambientRingPresheaf A).obj (op W) :=
  (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}).mapIso
    ((Thickening.restrictionStructureIso A.obj).app (op W))

/-- **The identification of the sections of the structure presheaf over a restriction is
compatible with restricting to a smaller open of the ambient scheme.** -/
theorem sectionsIso_restrictOpenLE (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    {W W' : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens} (h : W ≤ W') :
    (crisRing S).map (restrictOpenLE A h).op ≫ (sectionsIso A W).hom =
      (sectionsIso A W').hom ≫ (ambientRingPresheaf A).map (homOfLE h).op :=
  (((forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}).map_comp _ _).symm.trans
    (congrArg (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}).map
      ((Thickening.restrictionStructureIso A.obj).hom.naturality (homOfLE h).op))).trans
    ((forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}).map_comp _ _)

/-- **Under the identification of the sections of the structure presheaf over a restriction, the
map on sections of the structure morphism of that restriction is a restriction map of the
structure sheaf of the ambient scheme.** -/
theorem sectionsIso_restrictOpenHom (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    (W : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) :
    (crisRing S).map (A.restrictOpenHom W).op ≫ (sectionsIso A W).hom =
      (ambientRingPresheaf A).map (homOfLE (le_top : W ≤ ⊤)).op :=
  ((forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}).map_comp _ _).symm.trans
    (congrArg (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}).map
      (Thickening.structureSheaf_map_restrictOpenHom A.obj W))

/-- **The structure presheaf of the small crystalline site satisfies descent for the family of
restrictions of an object to an open cover of its ambient scheme.**  Its sections over the members
of the family are the sections of the structure sheaf of the ambient scheme over the members of the
open cover, compatibly with restriction, so this is the Zariski sheaf condition on that scheme. -/
theorem isSheafFor_restrictOpenCover (A : CrystallineThickening S) {I : Type (u + 1)}
    (V : I → A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)
    (hV : ∀ x : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ∃ i, x ∈ V i) (E : RingCat.{u}) :
    Presieve.IsSheafFor (crisRing S ⋙ coyoneda.obj (op E))
      (A.restrictOpenCover V).presieve₀ := by
  have hzar : Presieve.IsSheafFor (ambientRingPresheaf A ⋙ coyoneda.obj (op E))
      (Presieve.ofArrows V fun i ↦ homOfLE (le_top : V i ≤ ⊤)) := by
    rw [Presieve.isSheafFor_iff_generate]
    refine isSheaf_ambientRingPresheaf A E _ fun x _ ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hV x
    exact ⟨V i, homOfLE le_top, Sieve.le_generate _ _ _ ⟨i⟩, hi⟩
  have hpre : (A.restrictOpenCover V).presieve₀ =
      Presieve.ofArrows (fun i ↦ A.restrictOpen (V i)) fun i ↦ A.restrictOpenHom (V i) := rfl
  rw [hpre, Presieve.isSheafFor_arrows_iff]
  rw [Presieve.isSheafFor_arrows_iff] at hzar
  intro x hx
  have hcompat : Presieve.Arrows.Compatible (ambientRingPresheaf A ⋙ coyoneda.obj (op E))
      (fun i ↦ homOfLE (le_top : V i ≤ ⊤)) fun i ↦ x i ≫ (sectionsIso A (V i)).hom := by
    intro i j W gi gj _
    have hi : W ≤ V i := leOfHom gi
    have hj : W ≤ V j := leOfHom gj
    have key := hx i j (A.restrictOpen W) (restrictOpenLE A hi) (restrictOpenLE A hj)
      ((restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom A hi).trans
        (restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom A hj).symm)
    change (x i ≫ (sectionsIso A (V i)).hom) ≫ (ambientRingPresheaf A).map (homOfLE hi).op =
      (x j ≫ (sectionsIso A (V j)).hom) ≫ (ambientRingPresheaf A).map (homOfLE hj).op
    rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, ← sectionsIso_restrictOpenLE A hi,
      ← sectionsIso_restrictOpenLE A hj, ← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc]
    exact congrArg (fun m ↦ m ≫ (sectionsIso A W).hom) key
  obtain ⟨t, ht, huniq⟩ := hzar _ hcompat
  refine ⟨t, fun i ↦ ?_, fun t' ht' ↦ huniq t' fun i ↦ ?_⟩
  · change t ≫ (crisRing S).map (A.restrictOpenHom (V i)).op = x i
    refine (cancel_mono (sectionsIso A (V i)).hom).mp ?_
    exact ((Category.assoc _ _ _).trans (congrArg (fun m ↦ t ≫ m)
      (sectionsIso_restrictOpenHom A (V i)))).trans (ht i)
  · change t' ≫ (ambientRingPresheaf A).map (homOfLE (le_top : V i ≤ ⊤)).op =
      x i ≫ (sectionsIso A (V i)).hom
    exact ((congrArg (fun m ↦ t' ≫ m) (sectionsIso_restrictOpenHom A (V i))).symm.trans
      (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm).trans
        (congrArg (fun m ↦ m ≫ (sectionsIso A (V i)).hom) (ht' i))

end CrystallineThickening

/-- The coverage of `Cris(X/S)` whose covering presieves are the families of restrictions of an
object to an open cover of its ambient scheme; the restriction of a morphism over an open gives
the refinement needed for stability under pullback. -/
def restrictCoverage (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    Coverage (CrystallineThickening S) where
  coverings A := {R | ∃ (I : Type (u + 1)) (V : I → A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens),
    (∀ x : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ∃ i, x ∈ V i) ∧ R = (A.restrictOpenCover V).presieve₀}
  pullback := by
    rintro B A g R ⟨I, V, hV, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨(A.restrictOpenCover fun i ↦ g.hom.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ V i).presieve₀,
      ⟨I, _, fun x ↦ ?_, rfl⟩, ?_⟩
    · obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hV (g.hom.targetHom.hom.base x)
      exact ⟨i, hi⟩
    · rintro Z k ⟨i⟩
      exact ⟨B.restrictOpen (V i), CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenMap g (V i),
        B.restrictOpenHom (V i), ⟨i⟩,
        CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenMap_restrictOpenHom g (V i)⟩

/-- **A family of restrictions of an object of `Cris(X/S)` to an open cover of its ambient scheme
covers in the small crystalline site.** -/
theorem generate_mem_smallTopology_of_mem_restrictCoverage
    (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) {A : CrystallineThickening S} {R : Presieve A}
    (hR : R ∈ restrictCoverage S A) : Sieve.generate R ∈ smallTopology S A := by
  obtain ⟨I, V, hV, rfl⟩ := hR
  exact smallZariskiCovering_mem_smallTopology S _
    (CrystallineThickening.isZariskiCovering_restrictOpenCover A V hV)

/-- **A Zariski covering family of `Cris(X/S)` is refined by the family of restrictions of its
target to the images of the ambient schemes of its members**, hence generates a covering sieve for
the coverage of families of restrictions. -/
theorem generate_mem_restrictCoverage_toGrothendieck
    {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}} {B : CrystallineThickening S}
    (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} B) (hE : CrystallineThickening.IsZariskiCovering E) :
    Sieve.generate E.presieve₀ ∈ (restrictCoverage S).toGrothendieck B := by
  have hcart : ∀ i, Thickening.IsCartesian (E.f i).hom := hE.1
  have hE2 := hE.2
  simp only [Thickening.targetPresieve, Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff] at hE2
  have hoi : ∀ i, IsOpenImmersion (E.f i).hom.targetHom.hom := hE2.2
  refine Coverage.mem_toGrothendieck_sieves_of_superset _ (R :=
    (B.restrictOpenCover fun i ↦ (E.f i).hom.targetHom.hom.opensRange).presieve₀) ?_
    ⟨E.I₀, _, fun x ↦ ?_, rfl⟩
  · rintro Z k ⟨i⟩
    have := hoi i
    exact CrystallineThickening.restrictOpenHom_opensRange_mem_generate (E.f i) (hcart i) ⟨i⟩
  · obtain ⟨i, y, hy⟩ := hE2.1 x
    exact ⟨i, y, hy⟩

/-- **The Zariski topology of the small crystalline site is generated by the families of
restrictions of an object to an open cover of its ambient scheme.** -/
theorem restrictCoverage_toGrothendieck (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    (restrictCoverage S).toGrothendieck = smallTopology S := by
  refine le_antisymm (((Coverage.gi (CrystallineThickening S)).gc _ _).2 fun A R hR ↦
    generate_mem_smallTopology_of_mem_restrictCoverage S hR) ?_
  change (smallPrecoverage S).toGrothendieck ≤ _
  rw [Precoverage.toGrothendieck_eq_sInf]
  refine sInf_le ?_
  rintro A R ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩
  exact generate_mem_restrictCoverage_toGrothendieck E hE

/-- **The structure presheaf of the small crystalline site is a sheaf.**  Descent need only be
checked for the families of restrictions of an object to an open cover of its ambient scheme,
where it is the Zariski sheaf condition on that scheme. -/
theorem isSheaf_crisRing (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (smallTopology S) (crisRing S) := by
  rw [← restrictCoverage_toGrothendieck]
  intro E
  rw [Presieve.isSheaf_coverage]
  rintro A R ⟨I, V, hV, rfl⟩
  exact CrystallineThickening.isSheafFor_restrictOpenCover A V hV E

/-- The structure sheaf `𝒪_{X/S}` of the small crystalline site, the sheaf of rings sending an
object `(U, T, δ)` of `Cris(X/S)` to the ring of global sections `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)`. -/
def structureSheaf (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    Sheaf (smallTopology S) RingCat.{u} :=
  ⟨crisRing S, isSheaf_crisRing S⟩

/-- The underlying presheaf of `structureSheaf S` is `crisRing S`. -/
@[simp]
theorem structureSheaf_obj (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    (structureSheaf S).obj = crisRing S := rfl

/-- The structure presheaf of the small crystalline site, as a presheaf of commutative rings. -/
def structurePresheaf (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{u} :=
  (CrystallineThickening.ι S).op ⋙ GlobalCrystallineSituation.structureSheaf S

/-- **The structure presheaf of the small crystalline site is a sheaf of commutative rings.**  The
forgetful functor to rings is fully faithful, hence reflects limits, so this is the sheaf condition
for the underlying presheaf of rings. -/
theorem isSheaf_structurePresheaf (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (smallTopology S) (structurePresheaf S) :=
  Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _ _ (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})
    (isSheaf_crisRing S)

/-- The structure sheaf `𝒪_{X/S}` of the small crystalline site, as a sheaf of commutative
rings. -/
def commStructureSheaf (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    Sheaf (smallTopology S) CommRingCat.{u} :=
  ⟨structurePresheaf S, isSheaf_structurePresheaf S⟩

/-! ### The restrictions of an object as a morphism of sites -/

namespace CrystallineThickening

/-- A morphism into a restriction is determined by its composite with the structure morphism. -/
private theorem comp_restrictOpenLE_eq_of_comp_eq (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    {V V' : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens} (h : V ≤ V') {B : CrystallineThickening S}
    (p : B ⟶ A.restrictOpen V) (f : B ⟶ A.restrictOpen V')
    (hp : p ≫ A.restrictOpenHom V = f ≫ A.restrictOpenHom V') : p ≫ restrictOpenLE A h = f := by
  rw [← cancel_mono (A.restrictOpenHom V'), Category.assoc, restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom]
  exact hp

/-- **The restrictions of an object of `Cris(X/S)` to the opens of its ambient scheme preserve
covers:** a Zariski cover of an open `W` of the ambient scheme gives, after restricting, a covering
family of the restriction of the object to `W`.  Each member of the family of restrictions of
`A|_W` to the preimages of the members of the cover factors through the restriction of `A` to the
corresponding open. -/
theorem coverPreserving_restrictOpenFunctor (A : CrystallineThickening S) :
    CoverPreserving (Opens.grothendieckTopology A.obj.thickening.target.scheme)
      (smallTopology S) (restrictOpenFunctor A) where
  cover_preserve {W} {R} hR := by
    change Sieve.functorPushforward (restrictOpenFunctor A) R ∈
      smallTopology S (A.restrictOpen W)
    have hcov : ∀ x : (A.restrictOpen W).obj.thickening.target.scheme,
        ∃ i : ULift.{u + 1} (Σ' (V : A.obj.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) (h : V ≤ W),
            PLift (R.arrows (homOfLE h))),
          x ∈ (A.restrictOpenHom W).hom.targetHom.hom ⁻¹ᵁ i.down.1 := by
      intro x
      obtain ⟨V, m, hm, hxV⟩ := hR x.1 x.2
      exact ⟨⟨V, leOfHom m, ⟨hm⟩⟩, hxV⟩
    refine (smallTopology S).superset_covering ?_
      (generate_mem_smallTopology_of_mem_restrictCoverage S ⟨_, _, hcov, rfl⟩)
    rintro Z k ⟨Y, a, b, ⟨i⟩, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨i.down.1, homOfLE i.down.2.1,
      a ≫ restrictOpenMap (A.restrictOpenHom W) i.down.1, i.down.2.2.down, ?_⟩
    exact (congrArg (fun z ↦ a ≫ z) (comp_restrictOpenLE_eq_of_comp_eq A i.down.2.1 _ _
      (restrictOpenMap_restrictOpenHom _ _)).symm).trans (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm

/-- **The restrictions of an object of `Cris(X/S)` to the opens of its ambient scheme preserve
compatible families.**  Two morphisms out of an object of `Cris(X/S)` into the restrictions to two
opens which agree over a third one have the same composite to the object itself, so the ambient
scheme of their source maps into the intersection of the two opens; the universal property of the
restriction to that intersection then factors both through it, and compatibility over the
intersection gives the required equality. -/
theorem compatiblePreserving_restrictOpenFunctor (A : CrystallineThickening S) :
    CompatiblePreserving.{w} (smallTopology S) (restrictOpenFunctor A) where
  compatible := by
    intro ℱ Z Rp x hx Y₁ Y₂ B f₁ f₂ g₁ g₂ hg₁ hg₂ he
    obtain ⟨f₁, rfl⟩ : ∃ q : B ⟶ A.restrictOpen Y₁, q = f₁ := ⟨f₁, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨f₂, rfl⟩ : ∃ q : B ⟶ A.restrictOpen Y₂, q = f₂ := ⟨f₂, rfl⟩
    have he' : f₁ ≫ restrictOpenLE A g₁.le = f₂ ≫ restrictOpenLE A g₂.le := he
    have hcomp : f₁ ≫ A.restrictOpenHom Y₁ = f₂ ≫ A.restrictOpenHom Y₂ := by
      rw [← restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom A g₁.le,
        ← restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom A g₂.le, ← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc]
      exact congrArg (fun m ↦ m ≫ A.restrictOpenHom Z) he'
    have hmem : ∀ y : B.obj.thickening.target.scheme,
        (f₁ ≫ A.restrictOpenHom Y₁).hom.targetHom.hom.base y ∈ Y₁ ⊓ Y₂ := fun y ↦
      ⟨(f₁.hom.targetHom.hom.base y).2,
        (congrArg (fun m : B ⟶ A ↦ m.hom.targetHom.hom.base y) hcomp).symm ▸
          (f₂.hom.targetHom.hom.base y).2⟩
    obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := exists_comp_restrictOpenHom_eq (Y₁ ⊓ Y₂)
      (f₁ ≫ A.restrictOpenHom Y₁) hmem
    have h1 := comp_restrictOpenLE_eq_of_comp_eq A (inf_le_left (a := Y₁) (b := Y₂)) p f₁ hp
    have h2 := comp_restrictOpenLE_eq_of_comp_eq A (inf_le_right (a := Y₁) (b := Y₂)) p f₂
      (hp.trans hcomp)
    suffices h : ∀ (u₁ : ℱ.obj.obj (op (A.restrictOpen Y₁)))
        (u₂ : ℱ.obj.obj (op (A.restrictOpen Y₂))),
        ℱ.obj.map (restrictOpenLE A (inf_le_left (a := Y₁) (b := Y₂))).op u₁ =
            ℱ.obj.map (restrictOpenLE A (inf_le_right (a := Y₁) (b := Y₂))).op u₂ →
          ℱ.obj.map f₁.op u₁ = ℱ.obj.map f₂.op u₂ from
      h _ _ (hx (homOfLE (inf_le_left (a := Y₁) (b := Y₂)))
        (homOfLE (inf_le_right (a := Y₁) (b := Y₂))) hg₁ hg₂ rfl)
    intro u₁ u₂ hu
    rw [← h1, ← h2, op_comp, op_comp, Functor.map_comp_apply,
      Functor.map_comp_apply]
    exact congrArg (ℱ.obj.map p.op) hu

/-- **The restrictions of an object of `Cris(X/S)` to the opens of its ambient scheme form a
continuous functor** from the Zariski site of that scheme to the small crystalline site. -/
theorem restrictOpenFunctor_isContinuous (A : CrystallineThickening S) :
    (restrictOpenFunctor A).IsContinuous
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology A.obj.thickening.target.scheme) (smallTopology S) :=
  Functor.isContinuous_of_coverPreserving (compatiblePreserving_restrictOpenFunctor A)
    (coverPreserving_restrictOpenFunctor A)

/-- **The restrictions of an object of `Cris(X/S)` to the opens of its ambient scheme form a
cocontinuous functor** from the Zariski site of that scheme to the small crystalline site.  A
covering family of a restriction `A|_W` is, over the image in `W` of the open where a given member
has a factorization, refined by that member, and those images cover `W`. -/
theorem restrictOpenFunctor_isCocontinuous (A : CrystallineThickening S) :
    (restrictOpenFunctor A).IsCocontinuous
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology A.obj.thickening.target.scheme)
      (smallTopology S) := by
  refine Functor.isCocontinuous_toGrothendieck _ _ _ ?_
  rintro W B p R ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩
  obtain ⟨p, rfl⟩ : ∃ q : A.restrictOpen W ⟶ B, q = p := ⟨p, rfl⟩
  have hE2 := hE.2
  simp only [Thickening.targetPresieve, Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff] at hE2
  have hsurj : ∀ x : B.obj.thickening.target.scheme,
      ∃ i, ∃ y, (E.f i).hom.targetHom.hom.base y = x := hE2.1
  have hoi : ∀ i, IsOpenImmersion (E.f i).hom.targetHom.hom := hE2.2
  intro x hx
  obtain ⟨i, y, hy⟩ := hsurj (p.hom.targetHom.hom.base ⟨x, hx⟩)
  have := hoi i
  have hle : (A.obj.restrictOpenHom W).targetHom.hom ''ᵁ
      Thickening.pullbackOpen (E.f i).hom p.hom ≤ W := W.ι_image_le _
  obtain ⟨h, hh⟩ :=
    Thickening.exists_comp_eq_restrictOpenLE_image W p.hom (E.f i).hom (hE.1 i) hle
  refine ⟨_, homOfLE hle, ⟨E.X i, ObjectProperty.homMk h, E.f i, ⟨i⟩,
    ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ hh⟩, ?_⟩
  exact (W.mem_ι_image_iff (x := ⟨x, hx⟩)).mpr ⟨y, hy⟩

/-- **The restriction of a sheaf on the small crystalline site to the ambient scheme of an object
is a Zariski sheaf on that scheme.**  The coverings of `Cris(X/S)` are the Zariski coverings of the
ambient schemes, so the restrictions of an object to the opens of its ambient scheme form a
continuous functor and restriction along it carries sheaves to sheaves. -/
theorem isSheaf_restriction {𝒜 : Type v} [Category.{t} 𝒜] (A : CrystallineThickening S)
    (P : (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ 𝒜) (hP : Presheaf.IsSheaf (smallTopology S) P) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology A.obj.thickening.target.scheme)
      ((restrictOpenFunctor A).op ⋙ P) :=
  have := restrictOpenFunctor_isContinuous A
  Functor.op_comp_isSheaf_of_isSheaf _ _ _ P hP

end CrystallineThickening

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

